Package: bragi
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: NickMarcha <https://github.com/NickMarcha/bragi>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3.13, pipewire-bin, wireplumber, systemd, udev
Recommends: deskflow, bluez, tailscale
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/NickMarcha/bragi
Description: desk hub: shared headset, keyboard, mouse and controllers for several computers
 Bragi runs on a small box at the desk (a Raspberry Pi or a small x86
 server) and owns the shared devices: it mixes and routes a USB headset's
 audio to and from the computers over the network, switches the keyboard
 and mouse between them through the headless Deskflow server (package
 deskflow, optional), passes game controllers through, pairs Bluetooth
 devices, and serves a dashboard and an API for all of it.
 .
 It runs as a systemd user service (bragi.service) of the box's user, on
 127.0.0.1:8000; expose it with `tailscale serve`.
